  "result": "I fixed the inverted plan check in `src/server/services/search-service.ts`, but I haven't run the test suite.\n\nThe guard in `search()` was `input.q.includes(\":\") && advanced`, so it threw \"Field-scoped search is not included in this plan\" for plans that have `advanced_search`. Plans without it were never blocked. It now reads `input.q.includes(\":\") && !advanced`. Plain keyword searches don't contain a colon, so they were never affected.\n\nThe other search entry points (`src/app/api/search/route.ts`, `src/actions/search/search.ts` and the search page) only narrow which kinds get searched. They never reject a colon query, so they needed no change.",
